## What I built
**`courses/sar-…/lessons/radar-to-nie-kamera-wasne-oswietlenie-zamiast-swiata-otoczenia.json`** — 7 sections, intuition-first Polish, tuned to the binding audience override (senior CV eng, physics-light) and the 0.5 theory/practice ratio:
1. **theory** *Piksel to echo, nie kolor* (250 w) — active vs passive, backscatter, one glossed inline relation `$B \propto P_{\text{echo}}$`; **real optical (S2) + SAR (S1) Gibraltar pair** inline.
2. **quiz** — why calm water is black (specular reflection, not "dark colour").
3. **theory** *Co znika, a co się pojawia* (229 w) — optical→SAR change table + bridge to optical CV; inline real SAR zoom.
4. **plotImage** — echo-strength histogram of the real tile (two populations, threshold at 120), full axes/labels/title.
5. **code** — loads the genuine Sentinel-1 tile from `/inputs/`, thresholds echo strength into a strong-scatterer mask; 4 tests (1 visible), reference solution, live `outputMedia`.
6. **quiz** (multi-select) — consequences/misconceptions (all-weather, brightness≠size, corner reflectors, ImageNet-transfer caveat).
7. **sandbox** — free re-threshold on the same real tile.
**Real Copernicus data** (used the provided creds): Sentinel-1 GRD + Sentinel-2 L2A quicklooks over the Strait of Gibraltar → grayscale SAR hero, optical counterpart, a 256×256 SAR code tile, reference mask, and the histogram PNG — all under `assets/`.
