**`courses/…/lessons/od-sceny-do-kafelka-grd-multilooking-geokodowanie-i-terrain-correction.json`**
Section flow (`theory → plotImage → parametricExplorer → quiz → theory → code → sandbox`): 2 theory beats (245 / 195 words, not back-to-back) + 5 widgets, starts on theory, ends on a widget. Polish, intuition-first for the senior-CV / weak-physics learner, with RGB/RAW bridges throughout.
- **Theory 1** — SLC→GRD pipeline overview with a "po co" for each step + an SLC-vs-GRD comparison table; inline chain diagram.
- **plotImage** — slant-vs-ground geometry (Sentinel-1, H=693 km) with full labelled axes/units, showing why GRD *resamples* the scene.
- **ParametricExplorer** — multilooking looks-slider on a synthetic 1-look scene; ENL climbs 1→4→9→23→59 as resolution drops (the core trade-off, shown not told).
- **Quiz** (multi-select) — GRD/SLC, multilooking cost, the "slant→ground is just unit change" misconception, georeferencing for ship coordinates.
- **Theory 2** — Range-Doppler terrain correction with a DEM, layover correction, a homography/depth-map CV bridge, plus a non-runnable `snappy` reference graph; inline radar-grid-vs-map-grid diagram.
- **Code** — implement `multilook` (block-average) on the real Gibraltar tile mounted at `/inputs/`, graded on shape, block-mean, identity, and ENL gain; reference input + expected-output figures.
- **Sandbox** — free play with the looks count.
