**Lesson shape** (m6, 20 min, 0.5 theory/practice — balanced): 3 theory beats + 5 widgets, 8 sections total, starts on theory, ends on a quiz, no back-to-back theory:
1. **theory** — "Cała ścieżka w jednym pliku": the 5-stage end-to-end pipeline (scene→tile → land mask → CFAR → chips→classifier → report), with the runnable-core vs SNAP/PyTorch-reference split + inline pipeline-chain image.
2. **plotImage** — detection funnel (16384 px → 46 CFAR px → 18 candidates → 4 ships, log axis), generated fresh.
3. **quiz** (single) — why mask land *before* CFAR (clutter-statistics reasoning).
4. **theory** — what the report must contain (range/azimuth, class, confidence, geocoding), ships-vs-aircraft framing + inline result overlay.
5. **code** (graded) — `run_capstone` glues provided `ca_cfar`/`sea_mask`/`detect_targets` into a report dict; runs on the real Sentinel-1 tile in `/inputs/`, 4 tests (1 visible), full solution, live `outputMedia`, `requiresPackages: ["scipy"]`.
6. **sandbox** — independently tune `alpha` (CFAR sensitivity) and `min_peak` (classifier threshold).
7. **theory** — 1:1 mapping to the SATIM ATR role (near-real-time/ONNX, data-agnostic robustness) + inline F1-vs-incidence-angle figure.
8. **quiz** (multi) — final synthesis of the two-stage ATR pipeline.
